+## Portability successor v2
+
+Sealed v1 is preserved. `selector.py` and `PROTOCOL.json` are byte-identical to v1, including all scientific behavior and the 13 null prospective constants. The exact source/binding/test diff is saved in `DIFF_V1_V2.patch`.
+
+Every file descriptor in `SOURCE_BINDINGS.json` is now relative to the research phase. `driver.source_path` resolves it against `HERE.parent`; the native adapter identity check uses that same resolution. The four unchanged local native dependencies are bound and preloaded in their ordinary module names before native adapter use. Direct external numerical imports are listed separately and remain ordinary installed runtime dependencies pending qualification.
+
+The loader hashes and compiles the exact bound source bytes directly, so it neither reads nor writes donor bytecode caches. Its stdlib relocation test moves a phase tree, loads bound stub dependencies and a native-adapter stub from the new location, and checks that preexisting stale bytecode stays untouched even with bytecode writes globally enabled. No numerical source or real warm-state operation is executed by this test.
+
+For a future host, transfer this packet and its bound source donor subtrees while preserving their relative layout beneath the phase directory. All numerical, fresh-warm and predictive checks above remain pending root review and qualification; this portability repair grants none of them.
